  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "Admin.E108 is raised on fields accessible only via instance due to an issue in the ModelAdmin list_display validation. After upgrading Django from 2.0.7 to 2.2.1, configurations that previously passed now fail because the check in _check_list_display_item mistakenly relies on hasattr and does not even attempt to retrieve the field through model._meta.get_field. This causes valid cases\u2014such as those using fields like PositionField\u2014to be incorrectly flagged as erroneous. The fix requires revising the field resolution logic so that an error is only raised if both retrieval methods (via get_field and getattr) fail, while ManyToManyField cases continue to be properly handled.",
    "hint_texts": "Focus on modifying the django/contrib/admin/checks.py file. Update the _check_list_display_item method by removing the premature hasattr check and replacing it with a try/except mechanism that first calls model._meta.get_field, then falls back to getattr if needed. Ensure that if a field is successfully retrieved, no error is returned, and if the field is a ManyToManyField, the correct error (admin.E109) is raised.",
    "entrypoint": "File: django/contrib/admin/checks.py; Function: _check_list_display_item (starting around line 720). Developers should locate the block where hasattr(obj, item) is used and refactor it to use a try block for obj.model._meta.get_field(item), catching FieldDoesNotExist and then calling getattr as a fallback.",
