    "prompt": "A ModelAdmin that uses PositionField in its list_display now triggers an incorrect admin.E108 error, thereby preventing Django from starting. The issue arises because fields that are accessible only via an instance are being mistakenly rejected by the validation logic. The desired behavior is for the ModelAdmin to correctly resolve such fields using alternative lookup methods rather than immediately raising an error. In this way, valid configurations that use fields like PositionField pass the checks, while truly invalid setups continue to be flagged.",
    "hint_texts": "Implement a new test in tests/modeladmin/test_checks.py to ensure that a ModelAdmin with a PositionField in its list_display passes validation. The test should simulate a scenario where a field is only accessible via instance and verify that no admin.E108 error is raised. Make sure that this test fails with the old logic and passes once the new retrieval mechanism is in place.",
    "entrypoint": "File: tests/modeladmin/test_checks.py; Function: test_valid_field_accessible_via_instance. The new test should be added around line 509 as indicated in the diff, targeting the behavior of ModelAdmin when handling fields that require instance access.",
